@startuml sequence
title Service Discovery Sequence

skinparam sequenceParticipantBackgroundColor #F7F7F7
skinparam sequenceParticipantBorderColor #666666
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBorderColor #777777
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBackgroundColor #EFEFEF

participant "AppFactory" as Root #CFE8FF
participant "App" as App #CFE8FF
participant "ProxyNeedsFactory" as NeedsFactory
participant "ProxyNeeds" as Needs
participant "RequestedProxies" as Requested
participant "ProxyContainer" as Container
participant "ProxyBuilderBase" as Builder
participant "FindStrategy" as Strategy
participant "ProxyHolder" as Holder

[-> Root : Configure
Root -> NeedsFactory : Create<Strategies...>()
NeedsFactory --> Root : ProxyNeeds
Root -> App : Inject ProxyNeeds

activate App

App -> Needs : WithOnServiceFound(callback tuple)
App -> Needs : InitiateServiceDiscovery(stop_token?)

loop each ProxySpec in ProxyNeeds
Needs -> Builder : Build(stop_token?)
Builder -> Strategy : Find(builder_callback)
Strategy -> Holder : StartFindService(find_callback)
end

Needs --> App : RequestedProxies

alt contains mandatory ProxySpec
App -> Requested : WaitForMandatoryProxies(stop_token)
Requested --> App : ProxyContainer
else only optional/multiple ProxySpec
App -> Requested : GetProxyContainer()
Requested --> App : ProxyContainer
end

== ProxyContainer is Built & Service Discovery Initiated ==

note over App, Requested
App can stop service discovery only when it owns stop-capable ProxyData
(typically optional/multiple via Extract()).
Single/Variant follow mandatory semantics and do not expose explicit stop.
end note

alt App uses Extract() for ownership path
alt Single<Proxy>
App -> Container : Extract<Single>()
Container --> App : SingleInstanceHolder<Proxy>
else Multiple<Proxy>
App -> Container : Extract<Multiple>()
Container --> App : MultipleProxyData<Proxy>
else Optional<Proxy>
App -> Container : Extract<Optional>()
Container --> App : OptionalProxyData<Proxy>
else Variant<Proxy...>
App -> Container : Extract<Variant>()
Container --> App : variant<...>
end
else App uses Get() for non-owning path
alt Single<Proxy>
App -> Container : Get<Single>()
Container --> App : SingleInstanceHolder<Proxy>&
else Multiple<Proxy>
App -> Container : Get<Multiple>()
Container --> App : MultiInstanceHolder<Proxy>&
else Optional<Proxy>
App -> Container : Get<Optional>()
Container --> App : ProxyFuture<Proxy>&
else Variant<Proxy...>
App -> Container : Get<Variant>()
Container --> App : variant<...>
end
end

note over App, Container
Service discovery lifecycle is tied to internal stop action ownership.
For ownership-centric control, prefer Extract() for optional/multiple.
end note

deactivate App

@enduml
